## What is measured
- Motion: the largest mean |Δ| between consecutive sampled frames (t = {{ judge_times }}) must reach 0.002
  (else `static`, cap 0.5) and no consecutive pair may exceed 0.35 (`flicker`, cap 0.7): continuous motion,
  no hard cuts, no per-frame random seeds.
- Circles must stay round at {{ resolution }} (judge defect `stretched_aspect`, −0.06).
- The style's palette is what the judge's light_and_tone criterion grades against; no sampled frame may be
  essentially black or blown out (cap 0.5).
- Structure at the scales the subject has: one field filling the frame is the `flat_fill` defect (−0.08)
  and the 0.1 anchor of depth_and_detail (0.16).
- One NaN / Inf pixel caps the score at 0 (the NaN sources are listed in the contract).
- Loop bounds are compile-time constants; a frame that does not finish inside the render timeout fails the build.

## DON'T
- No `#version` line, no `uniform`/`out` declarations of the harness names (shader); no window,
  context creation, clock, file IO outside src/ (program).
- No placeholders ("TODO", "simplified"); no static image when the plan says motion.
- No textures other than the harness ones; no network; no imports outside the contract's allow-list.

